From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:40:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: allocate placeable host memory from the dma-heap
 biblioklept

VK_EXT_map_memory_placed maps memory at a caller-chosen address (Wine
WoW64 needs it below 4 GiB). kbase SAME_VA regions cannot be moved or
mapped twice, so the kbase backend used an anonymous shadow copy that
was merged word by word on every kick and wait. That was slow (i686
D3D9 at ~1 fps, Need for Speed Most Wanted at 0.5 fps) and racy (stale
DXVK HUD and game text).

When the app enables memoryMapPlaced, allocate host-visible memory as
shareable BOs. On kbase those come from /dev/dma_heap/system and are
imported into the GPU context; a placed map then maps the same dma-buf
again at the requested address, so CPU and GPU share pages with no
copy and no sync. The shadow copy is removed from kbase_kmod.c.

Purpose: zero-copy placed maps for 32-bit WoW64 (DXVK) on kbase
Source/Reference: VK_EXT_map_memory_placed; kbase_kmod.c dma-heap import path
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Poco X6 Pro)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 (MediaTek)
Mesa base range: 5a07217f034b (26.3.0-devel)
Dependencies: kbase-common kbase_kmod.c (dma-heap BOs, placed bo_mmap)
Validation test: i686 dxcube D3D8/9/10/11, Need for Speed Most Wanted (DXVK D3D9), dEQP-VK.memory.map_placed.*

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c
index 5e2b64e25e9..cf9f4c0aff8 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c
@@ -125,9 +125,16 @@ panvk_AllocateMemory(VkDevice _device,
           (type->propertyFlags & VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_CACHED_BIT))
          bo_flags |= PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_WB_MMAP;

+      /* A placed map aliases the BO at a caller-chosen address; on kbase
+       * only shareable (dma-buf backed) BOs can be mapped twice. */
+      bool shareable =
+         can_be_exported ||
+         (device->vk.enabled_features.memoryMapPlaced &&
+          (type->propertyFlags & VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_VISIBLE_BIT));
+
       bo_flags = panvk_device_adjust_bo_flags(device, bo_flags);
       mem->bo = pan_kmod_bo_alloc(device->kmod.dev,
-                                  can_be_exported ? NULL : device->kmod.vm,
+                                  shareable ? NULL : device->kmod.vm,
                                   pAllocateInfo->allocationSize, bo_flags);
       if (!mem->bo) {
          result = panvk_error(device, VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY);
